{\rtf\ansi \deff0{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue128;}{\fonttbl{\f0
\fcharset0\fnil Arial;}}\plain\cf1\fs20 \pard {\b Therefore, we 
conclude that in image processing applications, using a non-causal FIR 
filter makes the retrieved image easy to recognize as compared with 
the original image. If we use a causal filter the filtered image is 
translated image in the time domain. But this does not happen with the 
use of a causal filter.}}
